{
  "$comment": "Behaviour choreographies built from Knight clips. Each step plays a clip; looping clips run for `hold` seconds (random in [min,max]); one-shot clips play `repeat` times (default once) then hold their last frame for `hold` seconds if given. `until` ends a step on an external signal instead (e.g. 'woken'). `move` walks with a gait during the step (`turn`: clip played when the walk turns around). Steps ending on a `…ToIdle` clip hand over to idle without a snap. `interruptible: false` protects a step from being cut short. Tags feed the mood-driven AI; `requires` is checked before starting. `requires` is grounded | any | seat (perched on a window edge or at a bench; sitting clips are a front-facing pose with dangling legs). Weight 0 = never picked at random: the AI starts acts by name for a reason (watching activity, cursor above, mapping a new window, settling down, ...). Only `fidget` acts keep a small weight for genuine idle.",
